WEBVTT

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:03.492
Durvalumab, also called Imfinzi, is immunotherapy.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:06.812
This guide is for people receiving it on its own for stage three

00:00:06.812 --> 00:00:10.772
non-small cell lung cancer after chemotherapy and radiotherapy.

00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:15.652
Cancer cells can use a signal called PD-L1 to slow down immune cells.

00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:19.472
Durvalumab blocks that signal, helping immune cells attack cancer.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:22.552
Sometimes the immune system inflames healthy organs too.

00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:25.432
You receive a drip into a vein over about an hour.

00:00:25.772 --> 00:00:29.552
Visits are every two weeks or every four weeks, for up to a year.

00:00:30.012 --> 00:00:32.693
Your treatment card shows which schedule is yours.

00:00:32.992 --> 00:00:37.053
Before starting, your team checks blood counts, kidney and liver function,

00:00:37.053 --> 00:00:40.432
blood sugar, thyroid hormones and hepatitis B and C.

00:00:41.172 --> 00:00:43.812
A tumour test checks PD-L1.

00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:46.523
Repeat blood tests help spot changes early.

00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:49.912
Your team may also check cortisol if a hormone problem is suspected.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:53.203
Common effects include itching or rash, loose stools,

00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:56.932
cough, joint aches, fever and an underactive thyroid.

00:00:57.132 --> 00:01:00.383
Report changes early. If you feel unwell during an infusion,

00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:01.792
tell your nurse immediately.

00:01:02.032 --> 00:01:03.972
Pneumonitis means lung inflammation.

00:01:04.252 --> 00:01:08.592
Call your oncology team now for a new cough or more breathlessness, even if mild.

00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:12.272
The team may pause treatment, check for infection and give steroids.

00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:14.512
Colitis means bowel inflammation.

00:01:14.852 --> 00:01:17.372
Call now for more frequent or watery stools,

00:01:17.372 --> 00:01:19.732
tummy pain, or blood or mucus in your stool.

00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:22.792
You may need fluids, steroids and a treatment break.

00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:26.212
Hepatitis affects the liver. Nephritis affects the kidneys.

00:01:26.432 --> 00:01:29.232
Blood tests may pick these up before you feel unwell.

00:01:29.432 --> 00:01:34.152
Call now for yellow eyes, dark urine, passing much less urine or new swelling.

00:01:34.492 --> 00:01:38.492
Dermatitis means skin inflammation. Tell your team about a new rash.

00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:43.172
A spreading rash, blisters, peeling skin or mouth sores need urgent assessment.

00:01:43.452 --> 00:01:46.752
Thyroiditis can make the thyroid overactive, then underactive.

00:01:46.992 --> 00:01:51.103
Tiredness and feeling cold can be signs. An underactive thyroid is

00:01:51.103 --> 00:01:54.912
treated with hormone tablets called levothyroxine, sometimes for life.

00:01:55.212 --> 00:01:57.872
Many people can continue immunotherapy once stable.

00:01:58.192 --> 00:02:00.663
Adrenal insufficiency means too little cortisol.

00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:03.772
It can follow inflammation of the adrenal or pituitary glands.

00:02:03.972 --> 00:02:08.072
Call now for marked weakness, dizziness, vomiting or a persistent headache.

00:02:08.273 --> 00:02:12.312
Treatment may pause. Some people need lifelong hydrocortisone to replace cortisol.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.222
Other serious effects include myocarditis in the heart,

00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:19.372
myositis in muscles, nerve or brain inflammation, and type one diabetes.

00:02:19.712 --> 00:02:22.312
Call urgently for palpitations, new weakness,

00:02:22.312 --> 00:02:25.072
confusion, severe thirst or frequent urination.

00:02:25.472 --> 00:02:27.692
Eye and pancreas inflammation can occur too.

00:02:27.692 --> 00:02:30.332
Report changes even if they are not listed here.

00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:33.212
Problems can start months after the last dose.

00:02:33.212 --> 00:02:35.372
Some effects can cause permanent damage.

00:02:35.612 --> 00:02:37.712
Severe reactions can be life-threatening.

00:02:38.072 --> 00:02:40.972
Your team may use steroids or other medicines to calm

00:02:40.972 --> 00:02:43.732
inflammation and may stop immunotherapy permanently.

00:02:43.972 --> 00:02:48.472
Carry your immunotherapy alert card and save your twenty-four-hour oncology number.

00:02:48.472 --> 00:02:51.272
Call about new symptoms, even between visits.

00:02:51.532 --> 00:02:54.372
If you cannot reach the team, seek urgent care.

00:02:54.572 --> 00:03:00.792
For severe breathing difficulty, severe chest pain or collapse, call 112 or 999.
